       | --iissddeeeepp |  --iissnnoottddeeeepp  ]  [--ccmmaappoonnllyy]  [--aaddjjuussttccoolloorrss]  [--ttrraannssppaarreenntt
       _c_o_l_o_r] [--mmaasskkffiillee _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e [--vveerrbboossee] [_I_L_B_M_f_i_l_e]



DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       This program is part of NNeettppbbmm(1).

       iillbbmmttooppppmm  reads  an IFF ILBM file as input and produces a PPM image as
       output.  iillbbmmttooppppmm can handle the following ILBM types:



       •      Normal ILBMs with 1-16 planes.

       •      Amiga Extra_Halfbrite (EHB)

       •      Amiga HAM with 3-16 planes.

       •      24 bit.

       •      Multiplatte (normal or HAM) pictures.

       •      Color map (BMHD + CMAP chunk only, nPlanes = 0).

       •      Unofficial direct color.  1-16 planes for each color component.


       iillbbmmttooppppmm uses these ILBM chunks: BMHD, CMAP,  CAMG  (only  HAM  &  EHB
       flags  used), PCHG, BODY unofficial DCOL chunk to identify direct color
       ILBM.  It ignores these chunks: GRAB, DEST,  SPRT,  CRNG,  CCRT,  CLUT,
       DPPV,  DRNG,  EPSF.   It  ignores, but displays in verbose mode, these:
       NAME, AUTH, (c), ANNO, DPI.  It skips chunks whose type it doesn't rec‐
       ognize.


OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       In  addition  to  the options common to all programs based on libnetpbm
       (most notably --qquuiieett, see
        Common Options ⟨index.html#commonoptions⟩ ), iillbbmmttooppppmm recognizes  the
       following command line options:




       --ttrraannssppaarreenntt _c_o_l_o_r
              This is the color that should "show through" in places where the
              image is transparent.

              _c_o_l_o_r is like  the  argument  of  the  ppnnmm__ppaarrsseeccoolloorr(())  library
              routine ⟨libnetpbm_image.html#colorname⟩ .


       --vveerrbboossee
              Give some information about the ILBM file.


       --iiggnnoorree _c_h_u_n_k_I_D
              Skip  a  chunk.  _c_h_u_n_k_I_D is the 4-letter IFF chunk identifier of
              the chunk to be skipped.


       --iisshhaamm | --iisseehhbb
              Treat the input file as a HAM or Extra_Halfbrite  picture,  even
              if  these flags are not set in the CAMG chunk (or if there is no
              CAMG chunk).


       --mmaasskkffiillee _f_i_l_e_n_a_m_e
              This names a file for  iillbbmmttooppppmm  to  create  with  the  image's
              transparency  mask.   The mask file is a PBM image which maps to
              the input image with white pixels representing transparent  pix‐
              els in the image and black pixels representing opaque pixels.

              If  you  don't specfy this, or the image does not contain trans‐
              parency information, iillbbmmttooppppmm does not create a mask file.


       --ccmmaappoonnllyy
              With this option, iillbbmmttooppppmm generates a PPM of the ILBM's  _c_o_l_o_r
              _m_a_p, not the image itself.

              iillbbmmttooppppmm does the same thing even without --ccmmaappoonnllyy if the ILBM
              is a pure color map stream (it  has  a  bitmap  header  with  an
              _n_p_l_a_n_e_s value of zero or has no BODY chunk.


       --aaddjjuussttccoolloorrss
              If  all  colors  in the CMAP have a value of less then 16, ilbm‐
              toppm assumes a 4-bit colormap and gives a warning.   With  this
              option the colormap is scaled to 8 bits.





